# Public Marketplace Packaging Hygiene

This package is a **public** Cursor Marketplace / Grok Bot plugin. Treat every file, commit message, and PR description as public from day one.

## What to Avoid

**Never** include in plugin files, commit messages, PR bodies, or tool outputs:

- Private GitHub repository links or internal monorepo paths
- Internal issue, PR, or migration tracker IDs
- Lab, client, or internal brand names
- Authentication service internals (Cognito, account system details)
- Personal names, emails, or individual contributor attribution
- DEV, staging, or non-production hostnames
- "Private plugin" or "internal-only" framing language
- Engineering deployment workflows or infrastructure details

## What is Allowed

- **Product name:** WisePPC
- **Production MCP endpoint:** `https://mcp.wiseppc.com/mcp`
- **Public marketing URLs:** `wiseppc.com`, `app.wiseppc.com`, `wiseppc.com/ai-integration`
- **Public documentation** and marketplace-facing content
- Generic technical terminology (OAuth, API keys, datasets, etc.)

## Writing Guidelines

- Use marketplace-ready wording in README, skills, rules, CHANGELOG, and PR descriptions
- Frame features and changes from the **end user perspective** (what they can do, not how we built it)
- Keep technical implementation details focused on **public APIs and user-facing behavior**
- Do not document internal engineering workflows, private CI/CD systems, or company-specific processes
- When referencing version history or past work, use public commit SHAs or version tags only

## Commit & PR Standards

- **Commit messages:** Describe the change functionally, not the internal ticket that prompted it
- **PR titles:** Clear, public-safe feature or fix descriptions
- **PR bodies:** Follow PR templates if present; no internal links or private context

## When in Doubt

If you're unsure whether something is public-safe, assume it's internal and omit it. Better to be conservative than to leak private details into public marketplace distribution.
